{"id": "pandemic-relief-with-no-names", "title": "The City’s largest pandemic grant replaced its own revenue; its rent-aid reports disagree", "seconds": 156.8, "voice": "elevenlabs:iPYqcpY8j8Ap4jUf28I3", "narrator": "Michael", "tempo": 1.2, "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "bd724ab07ce5fa87", "words": 413, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "In the pandemic, Washington sent cities big streams of money. The rule: report back where it went.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 6.76, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Pandemic money from Washington", "sub": "a relief fund, a recovery grant, rent aid"}, "emph": ["report back"], "wt": [0.0, 0.04, 0.15, 1.13, 1.67, 1.93, 2.3, 2.6, 3.0, 3.14, 3.69, 4.17, 4.68, 5.5, 5.84, 6.0, 6.17]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["oneLine"], "text": "So how much of San Francisco’s money has no name next to it?", "t0": 6.88, "t1": 10.19, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "Who got paid?", "sub": "the City’s two largest pandemic grants"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.27, 0.4, 0.5, 0.69, 1.23, 1.53, 1.83, 1.99, 2.37, 2.63, 2.78]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["oneLine", "amount"], "text": "741.7 million dollars.", "t0": 10.19, "t1": 14.08, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$741.7 million", "label": "with no named recipient", "sub": "of $778.6 million"}, "emph": ["741.7"], "wt": [0.04, 0.9, 1.14, 1.73, 2.37, 2.62, 3.21]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["caveat"], "text": "This is a lead, not a finding.", "t0": 14.6, "t1": 16.54, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.18, 0.3, 1.04, 1.18, 1.28]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "share", "ref": ["oneLine"], "text": "That’s 95 percent of its two largest grants. No one is named as the one who got it.", "t0": 16.66, "t1": 22.53, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "share", "pct": 95, "label": "of the money, no recipient named"}, "emph": ["95 percent"], "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.73, 1.28, 1.51, 1.73, 1.98, 2.4, 3.33, 3.89, 4.04, 4.2, 4.7, 4.94, 5.04, 5.23, 5.38, 5.59]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]"], "text": "The first lead is the relief fund. Why did the City get 153.8 million dollars?", "t0": 22.75, "t1": 29.5, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "The relief fund", "kicker": "The first lead", "chip": "$153.8 million"}, "emph": ["153.8 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.06, 0.46, 0.84, 1.07, 1.19, 1.64, 2.22, 2.96, 3.07, 3.19, 3.49, 3.66, 3.89, 4.2, 4.85, 5.17, 5.47, 6.05]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "It was federal relief, sent from Washington. In return, the City had to say who it paid.", "t0": 29.5, "t1": 35.29, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "money", "name": "U.S. Treasury", "sub": "pandemic relief"}, {"art": "cityhall", "name": "City and County", "sub": "spends it"}, {"art": "question", "name": "One line, no recipient", "sub": "who was paid?"}], "kicker": "The first lead"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.61, 0.76, 1.17, 1.8, 1.95, 2.16, 2.97, 3.45, 4.01, 4.15, 4.34, 4.46, 4.57, 4.86, 5.17, 5.39]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "Then the recovery grant.", "t0": 35.41, "t1": 37.01, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "The recovery grant", "kicker": "The first lead", "chip": "$624.8 million"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.34, 0.59, 1.07]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "624.8 million dollars, on a single line.", "t0": 37.13, "t1": 42.07, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "The recovery grant", "kicker": "The first lead", "chip": "$624.8 million"}, "emph": ["single line"], "wt": [0.0, 0.24, 0.56, 1.21, 1.67, 2.09, 2.79, 3.78, 4.1, 4.18, 4.55]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "Other big California cities named 1,417 grants they passed on.", "t0": 42.19, "t1": 47.59, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Named subawards, by mid-2023", "rows": [["30 other large California cities and counties", "1417"], ["San Francisco", "0"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.5, 1.03, 1.35, 1.87, 2.17, 2.58, 2.83, 3.19, 3.87, 4.36, 4.58, 5.03]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "San Francisco named none.", "t0": 47.71, "t1": 49.72, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Named subawards, by mid-2023", "rows": [["30 other large California cities and counties", "1417"], ["San Francisco", "0"]]}, "emph": ["none"], "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.84, 1.51]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[2]", "suspicious[0].why", "notEstablished[4]"], "text": "Its label: public-safety revenue replacement.", "t0": 49.84, "t1": 53.06, "shot": "b11b", "visual": {"type": "doc", "kicker": "U.S. Treasury, April 2026 release", "text": "Revenue Replacement · 6.1-Provision of Government Services · Public Safety Revenue Replacement · Submitted Closeout Complete", "mark": "Public Safety Revenue Replacement"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.67, 1.94, 2.41]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[2]", "suspicious[0].why", "notEstablished[4]"], "text": "It paid for City services, so there’s no outside recipient.", "t0": 53.18, "t1": 56.28, "shot": "b11b", "visual": {"type": "doc", "kicker": "U.S. Treasury, April 2026 release", "text": "Revenue Replacement · 6.1-Provision of Government Services · Public Safety Revenue Replacement · Submitted Closeout Complete", "mark": "Public Safety Revenue Replacement"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.33, 0.48, 0.77, 1.61, 1.71, 1.92, 2.02, 2.49]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]"], "text": "The second lead is rent aid. The City said it spent 25.4 million dollars.", "t0": 56.5, "t1": 62.12, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Emergency rent aid", "kicker": "The second lead", "chip": "$25.4 million"}, "emph": ["25.4 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.43, 0.81, 1.1, 1.45, 2.06, 2.42, 2.67, 2.85, 2.96, 3.33, 3.87, 4.15, 4.43, 4.96]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what"], "text": "It helped 2,211 households,", "t0": 62.24, "t1": 65.67, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "2,211", "label": "households helped, $7,021 each on average"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.39, 0.65, 1.22, 1.56, 1.91, 2.31]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what"], "text": "about 7,021 dollars each.", "t0": 65.67, "t1": 68.91, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "2,211", "label": "households helped, $7,021 each on average"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.5, 0.89, 1.45, 2.23, 2.78]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what"], "text": "Multiply that out. What do you get?", "t0": 69.03, "t1": 71.31, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "2,211", "label": "households helped, $7,021 each on average"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.36, 0.64, 1.01, 1.46, 1.54, 1.69]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what"], "text": "15.5 million dollars.", "t0": 71.31, "t1": 74.47, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$15.5 million", "label": "households times average aid", "sub": "61% of what was spent"}, "emph": ["15.5"], "wt": [0.04, 1.17, 1.61, 1.9, 2.5]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "established[3]", "notEstablished[1]", "innocent[3]"], "text": "That’s 61 percent.", "t0": 74.99, "t1": 76.83, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "versus", "kicker": "The Treasury’s quarterly rent-aid file", "a": ["to households", "$19.4 million"], "b": ["administration, 16% of the grant", "$4.3 million"], "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.38, 1.22]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "established[3]", "notEstablished[1]", "innocent[3]"], "text": "Another Treasury file puts 4.3 million dollars on administration: 16 percent of the grant.", "t0": 76.95, "t1": 83.12, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "versus", "kicker": "The Treasury’s quarterly rent-aid file", "a": ["to households", "$19.4 million"], "b": ["administration, 16% of the grant", "$4.3 million"], "arrows": false}, "emph": ["4.3 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.28, 0.65, 1.03, 1.29, 1.57, 1.93, 2.09, 2.51, 2.99, 3.09, 4.56, 5.02, 5.39, 5.46, 5.58]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what"], "text": "San Francisco is the lowest of 36.", "t0": 83.24, "t1": 85.9, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Households × aid, as a share of spending", "rows": [["Median of 35 other grantees", "90"], ["Lowest other: Stanislaus County", "81"], ["San Francisco", "61"]]}, "emph": ["lowest of 36"], "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.78, 0.94, 1.1, 1.55, 1.81]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["established[4]", "notEstablished[3]"], "text": "City audits say other groups handed out the rent aid. Four are named, for 7.4 million.", "t0": 86.02, "t1": 91.56, "shot": "b16b", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Rent aid through the City, named in recipients’ own audits", "rows": [["Eviction Defense Collaborative", "$6.0 million"], ["Native American Health Center", "$1.0 million"], ["San Francisco Study Center", "$196,392"], ["Chinatown Community Development Center", "$190,000"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.26, 0.65, 0.83, 1.05, 1.37, 1.63, 1.75, 1.85, 2.12, 2.97, 3.18, 3.4, 4.17, 4.3, 4.53, 4.89, 5.06]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]"], "text": "The third lead is paycheck loans. That was federal money to keep staff paid.", "t0": 91.78, "t1": 95.92, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Paycheck-protection loans", "kicker": "The third lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.39, 0.64, 0.78, 1.27, 1.89, 2.3, 2.44, 2.78, 3.02, 3.11, 3.32, 3.67]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]"], "text": "If it was spent on pay, the loan was forgiven. It never had to be paid back.", "t0": 96.04, "t1": 101.51, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Paycheck-protection loans", "kicker": "The third lead", "sub": "spent on pay: forgiven, never paid back"}, "emph": ["forgiven"], "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.17, 0.31, 0.58, 0.8, 1.48, 1.59, 1.83, 1.98, 2.89, 3.37, 3.57, 3.69, 3.78, 3.92, 4.2]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what"], "text": "9 groups the City pays had big forgiven loans. And other federal emergency money too.", "t0": 101.63, "t1": 106.82, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "9", "label": "City payees with a forgiven loan and another federal emergency source"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.54, 0.63, 0.88, 1.3, 1.54, 1.84, 2.39, 3.02, 3.56, 3.83, 4.17, 4.62, 4.87]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[2].why"], "text": "Two programs at once isn’t the problem.", "t0": 106.94, "t1": 108.91, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Charging the same payroll to two of them is not"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.64, 0.8, 1.12, 1.35, 1.46]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[2].why"], "text": "Charging the same payroll to both would be. Only their books can show which.", "t0": 109.03, "t1": 113.25, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Charging the same payroll to two of them is not"}, "emph": ["same payroll"], "wt": [0.0, 0.3, 0.44, 0.66, 1.09, 1.2, 1.5, 1.73, 2.12, 2.9, 3.12, 3.45, 3.63, 3.8]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]"], "text": "The fourth lead is loan size. A loan was about 2.5 months of payroll.", "t0": 113.47, "t1": 118.32, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Loans bigger than the payroll", "kicker": "The fourth lead"}, "emph": ["2.5 months"], "wt": [0.0, 0.06, 0.36, 0.73, 1.02, 1.38, 2.26, 2.61, 2.86, 3.0, 3.26, 3.41, 3.72, 3.87, 4.18, 4.28]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what"], "text": "7 loans point to at least 1.25 times the biggest payroll the group ever reported.", "t0": 118.44, "t1": 124.77, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "7", "label": "loans implying at least 1.25 times the largest payroll reported"}, "emph": ["1.25 times"], "wt": [0.0, 0.34, 0.78, 1.07, 1.24, 1.38, 1.68, 1.99, 2.33, 2.6, 2.94, 3.45, 3.84, 4.2, 4.72, 4.91, 5.2, 5.53]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what"], "text": "The widest gap is Filipino-American Development Foundation.", "t0": 124.89, "t1": 128.17, "shot": "b24", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["payroll the loan implies", "$1.9 million"], "b": ["payroll on its return", "$792,725"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.47, 0.76, 1.02, 2.11, 2.59]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what"], "text": "Its loan points to 1.9 million dollars of payroll.", "t0": 128.29, "t1": 131.59, "shot": "b24", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["payroll the loan implies", "$1.9 million"], "b": ["payroll on its return", "$792,725"]}, "emph": ["1.9 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.48, 0.81, 0.95, 1.17, 1.53, 1.69, 2.09, 2.55, 2.7]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what"], "text": "Its tax return shows 792,725.", "t0": 131.71, "t1": 136.04, "shot": "b24", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["payroll the loan implies", "$1.9 million"], "b": ["payroll on its return", "$792,725"]}, "emph": ["792,725"], "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.44, 0.84, 1.18, 1.55, 1.84, 2.37, 2.85, 3.22, 3.5]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[3]"], "text": "Not shown: that any money was misspent,", "t0": 136.26, "t1": 139.12, "shot": "b26", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That any relief money was misspent", "Who handed out $18.4 million of the rent aid"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.25, 0.72, 1.29, 1.43, 1.71, 1.91]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[3]"], "text": "or who handed out 18.4 million of the rent aid.", "t0": 139.12, "t1": 144.39, "shot": "b26", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That any relief money was misspent", "Who handed out $18.4 million of the rent aid"]}, "wt": [0.04, 0.2, 0.44, 0.78, 0.97, 1.37, 1.65, 1.93, 2.55, 2.88, 3.0, 3.35]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[1]"], "text": "What would settle it? The ledger entries behind those lines.", "t0": 144.51, "t1": 148.18, "shot": "b27", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "Ledger entries behind the unnamed lines"}, {"who": "", "what": "The housing office’s list of rent-aid subrecipients"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.31, 0.64, 1.0, 1.65, 2.06, 2.51, 2.84, 3.14]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status", "sources"], "text": "The U.S. Treasury accepted these reports. No audit finding on them is on file.", "t0": 148.3, "t1": 153.25, "shot": "b28", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.46, 1.0, 1.55, 1.73, 2.62, 2.99, 3.31, 3.64, 3.77, 4.06, 4.37, 4.54]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "A lead is a question, not an accusation.", "t0": 153.37, "t1": 155.89, "shot": "b29", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.37, 0.44, 0.54, 1.23, 1.62, 1.78]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The question", "found": "On the record", "lead1": "Lead 1 · the unnamed lines", "lead2": "Lead 2 · rent aid", "lead3": "Lead 3 · two federal sources", "lead4": "Lead 4 · loans vs. payroll", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "dossier", "hook": "number"}